+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 A `ts` and a `typescript` code block in Markdown print `<T>(value: T) => {}` without the trailing comma after the lone type parameter (tests/format/markdown/code/ts-trailing-comma.md) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 A `tsx` code block in the same file keeps `<T,>(value: T) => {}`, and the existing `tsx-trailing-comma.md` and `typescript/tsx/comma` snapshots stay unchanged (tests/format/markdown/code/__snapshots__/jsfmt.spec.js.snap) [AC-2]
+
+## 2. Fix
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Decide whether the code may be tsx before forcing the comma: for code embedded in another file, by the file path the embedding printer gives it (src/language-js/print/type-parameters.js)
+- [ ] 2.2 Changelog entry (changelog_unreleased/markdown/15286.md)
